<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Somerset</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Somerset is a county of south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bristol">Bristol</a> Channel and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorset">Dorset</a>, with its county town at Taunton. Its low-lying Somerset Levels include the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athelney">Athelney</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a> sheltered from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> in 878, and the town of Glastonbury with its ancient abbey. The county was taken into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> in the 7th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/somerset.jpg" alt="Somerset" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puente_Pulteney,_Bath,_Inglaterra,_2014-08-12,_DD_51.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
